From 03b53780c65a95b0e2c70b7ca8f46f0a1370ccb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:33:44 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/33] managemon: do not use an array manage_member() may have
 freed

After manage_member(), manage() reads a->container to decide whether
the array needs manage_new().  manage_member() may have freed it by
then.  It changes an array by putting a copy in its place with
replace_array(), and each replace_array() first frees the array that
the previous one took out, once the monitor has let go of it.  So when
one pass replaces the array twice, the second replace_array() frees
the array that manage() holds.

Since commit 07ad253044f5 ("mdmon: delegate removal to managemon")
that happens whenever a member fails while the container has a spare:
once the monitor has stopped using the faulty device, one pass removes
it (replace_array(), then a = newa) and goes on to add the spare
(replace_array() again).  A level change, which replaces the array in
the same way since commit 57f8c76946f0 ("Detect level change"), can do
it too when a spare or new devices follow in the same pass.

With glibc the freed array is normally left as it was until manage()
reads it, so the stale a->container is not NULL and nothing visible
happens.  With an allocator that clears freed memory, a NULL there
would pass the freed array to manage_new() as the one to replace, and
replace_array() would hand it to the monitor and free it again.

Seen with AddressSanitizer: IMSM RAID1 with a spare in the container
on loop devices (IMSM_NO_PLATFORM=1), mdmon built with
-fsanitize=address, "mdadm --fail" of a member: heap-use-after-free in
manage() of the array freed by free_aa() from replace_array() in
manage_member(), and mdmon aborts after the spare has been added.  With
the change there is no report, and the spare is added the same way.

Decide whether the array is new before manage_member() is called, and
do not look at it afterwards.  An array the monitor deactivates while
manage_member() runs is now given to manage_new() on the next pass,
not in this one.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.

Fixes: 07ad253044f5 ("mdmon: delegate removal to managemon")
---
 managemon.c | 18 ++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/managemon.c b/managemon.c
index 8e74154c..fc7214e5 100644
--- a/managemon.c
+++ b/managemon.c
@@ -870,14 +870,20 @@ void manage(struct mdstat_ent *mdstat, struct supertype *container)
 			/* Not for this array */
 			continue;
 		/* Looks like a member of this container */
-		for (a = container->arrays; a; a = a->next) {
-			if (strcmp(mdstat->devnm, a->info.sys_name) == 0) {
-				if (a->container && a->to_remove == 0)
-					manage_member(mdstat, a);
+		for (a = container->arrays; a; a = a->next)
+			if (strcmp(mdstat->devnm, a->info.sys_name) == 0)
 				break;
-			}
+		if (a && a->container) {
+			/*
+			 * manage_member() may replace the array twice (a
+			 * device removed, then a spare added), and the second
+			 * replace_array() frees it: do not look at a after it.
+			 */
+			if (a->to_remove == 0)
+				manage_member(mdstat, a);
+			continue;
 		}
-		if ((a == NULL || !a->container) && !sigterm)
+		if (!sigterm)
 			manage_new(mdstat, container, a);
 	}
 }
